family: net-snmp
what: poll
transport: v3
address: 2001:db8::10
verification: tested
verification_detail: CI starts from a distribution-style snmpd.conf (agentaddress 127.0.0.1,[::1]), replaces that line and adds the rest as the snippet says, then Woodshed polls real snmpd, v2c and v3 (SHA-256 where the tools have it, and SHA-1 with another user name), and v2c over IPv6.
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (agentaddress, rocommunity, rocommunity6, createUser, rouser)
does: Lets Woodshed poll this machine's snmpd (SNMPv3, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with this machine's name and interfaces; after the first cycle the device page shows its graphs.
placeholders: <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Then add this machine in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, port 161, SNMPv3 and the user monitor; Test poll shows what answers.
- Add the same user in Woodshed first: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name monitor, SHA-256 and AES-128, with the same passphrases (at least 8 characters each).
- Some distributions want createUser in snmpd's persistent file (often /var/lib/snmp/snmpd.conf) instead, written while snmpd is stopped; their net-snmp-create-v3-user tool does that.
- Edit the agentaddress line rather than adding a second one: snmpd joins every agentaddress line it reads, so the distribution's usual `agentaddress 127.0.0.1,[::1]` would stay, and two entries for port 161 can stop snmpd from starting. The new line listens on every address, IPv4 and IPv6; to keep loopback-only addresses too, list them on the same line, comma-separated.
- Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only: it holds the passphrases.
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Replace the existing agentaddress line with this one (add it if there's none)
agentaddress udp:161,udp6:161
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Then add these lines to the same file, and restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd)
# Woodshed: answer polls (SNMPv3, read-only).
createUser monitor SHA-256 <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> AES <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
rouser monitor priv
==== text
# /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf: Replace the existing agentaddress line with this one (add it if there's none)
agentaddress udp:161,udp6:161

# /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf: Then add these lines to the same file, and restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd)
# Woodshed: answer polls (SNMPv3, read-only).
createUser monitor SHA-256 <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> AES <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
rouser monitor priv
